    pr_ref:  # f77f
    description: "sketch._collect_important_files.walk_additional_files (sketch.py ~L3597) filters rglob results with `any(fnmatch(p, pat) for p in item.parts for pat in excludes)` -- item.parts of an rglob result are ABSOLUTE path parts, so DEFAULT_EXCLUDES entries (.cache, build, dist, vendor, ...) match directories ABOVE the repo root. A repo checked out anywhere under a directory with an excluded name (e.g. ~/.cache/..., /srv/build/..., /home/me/vendor/...) gets zero additional-file candidates. Evidence (2026-10-07, while testing WI-vosag): running smart-test with TMPDIR=/home/jgstern_agent/.cache/hg-smarttest-tmp left sketch.py lines 3610-3613 and 3622-3632 (the candidate loop) uncovered -- every tmp_path fixture file was excluded by '.cache' in its absolute parts; with TMPDIR=/home/jgstern_agent/hg-smarttest-tmp the same tests cover them. Fix: match excludes against item.relative_to(repo_root).parts (and audit other `.parts` exclude checks for the same absolute-vs-relative mistake). The `file_index` branch (only via run_behavior_map) is pragma'd and not affected the same way. Also note that tests are sensitive to TMPDIR location because of this."  # f77f
    fields: {}  # f77f
